WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
Now, say a project

2
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.500
like Harbor Walk can't make

3
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.140
the numbers work

4
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:04.960
on its own.

5
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.940
Cities have a few

6
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.000
tools that can help

7
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.780
it move forward. One

8
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.080
is a tax break.

9
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:10.700
Instead of paying

10
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.460
full property taxes,

11
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.080
the owner pays

12
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.600
a smaller set amount

13
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.140
for a number

14
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.000
of years.

15
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.860
You'll often hear this

16
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.180
called a pilot.

17
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.300
It's short for payment

18
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.610
in lieu of taxes.

19
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.420
in lieu, that just

20
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.840
means instead of.

21
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.520
Another tool is low-cost

22
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.460
money or land.

23
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.540
A city might offer

24
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.200
a loan at

25
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.240
a lower interest rate

26
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.700
or sell or lease

27
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.790
land for less.

28
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:32.980
a third

29
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.860
is a zoning bonus.

30
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.840
The project may build

31
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.760
more homes than

32
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.170
the usual rules allow.

33
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.360
Each of these

34
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.760
is public support.

35
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.320
It has real value.

36
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.700
So the public usually

37
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.580
asks for something

38
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.290
in return.

